Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:45:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Vulkan FG-input feed: GPU relay, Reflex-sleep throttle,
 module-scan fix

The serial feed parks Streamline's FG command buffer on the CPU while the
real frame's NR runs, so generated frames cannot present in that window
(~59 of ~107 presents/s reached the screen in the game test). Pipeline=2
with Import=1 makes the copies the add-on's own Vulkan batch and releases
the park on the GPU through a shared D3D12 fence imported as a timeline
semaphore; VK_KHR_external_semaphore_win32 is appended at the ReShade
layer's vkCreateDevice. Throttle holds the game after slReflexSleep until
the newest armed frame's NR is done, because Reflex cannot see the private
D3D12 queue (PC latency p50 246 -> 158 ms, real frame rate unchanged).

ngx-module-scan.h references only modules that export an NGX pair; the
old scan held a reference on RenoDX Generic long enough for ReShade to
unregister it after the final instance was created (reproduced offline).
